### new
cicada new <name>

create an edition-2 project

Flags:
  (no command flags)
  --help      show this help

### bundle
cicada bundle <score.cicada> <bundle.zip>

package a portable score with provenance

Flags:
  (no command flags)
  --help      show this help

Copies score sources, referenced audio, pinned libraries, and Save As recovery files into a ZIP with a SHA-256 file inventory. Existing output files are refused.

### apply
cicada apply <score.cicada> <intents.json> [--write] [--author <name>] [--session <id>]

apply typed edit intents to a score

Flags:
  --write         write the validated edits (default: print a diff only)
  --author <name>  commit author (default: envelope author or cli)
  --session <id>   commit session
  --help          show this help

A supplied revision must match the score. Writes also check for concurrent saves. An envelope with dryrun:true never writes.

### fix
cicada fix <score.cicada> [--all] [--check]

migrate legacy source spellings

Flags:
  --all       migrate every edition-1 score under the project folder together
  --check     report required source or manifest changes without writing
  --help      show this help

With --all, the score path is optional; run the command from the project folder.

### check
cicada check [--profile desktop|browser] [--max-resident-pcm <size>] [score.cicada]

validate one score or the current project

Flags:
  --profile <name>           limits to check against: desktop (default) or browser
  --max-resident-pcm <size>  cap on decoded sampler-pack PCM, as for render, such as 2GiB (default 1GiB)
  --help                     show this help

The browser profile also builds the images cicada wam2 exports and applies the portable limits: 16 tracks, 32 allocated voices, a 2 MiB image and no master processor. It lists the voices each track reserves and fails when a limit is exceeded. For a score with sampler packs, check reads each pack's manifest, loads the packs one at a time, and reports a pack that does not load at 44.1, 48 or 96 kHz, a note outside every zone of its pack, and packs whose declared size render would refuse. Pack paths resolve from the folder of cicada.mod, as audio assets do. CICADA_MAX_RESIDENT_PCM sets the cap when the option is omitted.

### fmt
cicada fmt [--check|-w] [score.cicada]

format a score or current project

Flags:
  --check     report formatting changes without writing
  -w          write formatted source
  --help      show this help

### play
cicada play [score.cicada] [--audio tymbal|oto|null] [--max-resident-pcm <size>]

play and watch a score

Flags:
  --audio <name>             select tymbal, oto, or null
  --max-resident-pcm <size>  cap on decoded sampler-pack PCM held in memory, such as 512MiB (default 1GiB)
  --help                     show this help

CICADA_AUDIO selects the backend when --audio is omitted. Tymbal is the default on Windows and Linux; oto is the macOS default. Use --audio oto to select oto explicitly. Sampler packs stay in memory as decoded float32 PCM, and --max-resident-pcm caps their total; a score whose packs decode to more is refused, with the cap and the size measured in the message. A reloaded score reuses the packs already in memory; a reload that points a sampler at another pack holds both until the new score takes over at the next bar. CICADA_MAX_RESIDENT_PCM sets the cap when the option is omitted. Sizes are whole numbers with KiB, MiB, GiB, TiB, KB, MB, GB or TB, such as 512MiB.

### studio
cicada studio [score.cicada] [--listen 127.0.0.1:port] [--audio tymbal|oto|null] [--lsp-stdio] [--max-resident-pcm <size>]

open the local workstation

Flags:
  --listen <addr>            loopback address; default 127.0.0.1:0
  --audio <name>             select tymbal, oto, or null
  --lsp-stdio                serve LSP on stdin/stdout and Studio on stderr
  --max-resident-pcm <size>  cap on decoded sampler-pack PCM held in memory, such as 2GiB (default 1GiB)
  --help                     show this help

CICADA_AUDIO selects the backend when --audio is omitted. Tymbal is the default on Windows and Linux; oto is the macOS default. Use --audio oto to select oto explicitly. CICADA_MAX_RESIDENT_PCM sets the sampler-pack cap when --max-resident-pcm is omitted.

